te_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-10-04T00:28:07Z","updated_at":"2026-10-16T18:42:04Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in 4.7.2, e7cfa294\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.2.stable - SteamOS holo on Wayland - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Mobile) - integrated Turnip Adreno (TM) 750 -  (8 threads) - 15.29 GiB memory - PulseAudio (44100 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nOn the steam frame, eye tracked foveation (maybe all foveation?) only seems to work when FXAA is enabled. I've been told that's because FXAA disables subpasses.\n\n<img width=\"1920\" height=\"1080\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9d2ee6c8-eff3-4303-9b70-497f88b62da8\" />\n\nAbove with FXAA enabled, I am looking at the left of the screenshot, so the right is low res. The performance benefits of foveation are there with it running stable-ish at 36 fps.\n\n<img width=\"1920\" height=\"1080\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/23a075e6-de3f-4c7a-aa14-5422e77ffe93\" />\n\nWith FXAA disabled and no other changes to the project, the entire image is the same res and the performance benefits of foveation are not seen with it running at 24 fps.\n\nSeems unrelated to #113778 even though both are related to foveation and subpasses.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nRun the MRP project on the steam frame, take a screenshot, see that foveation isn't doing anything. Turn FXAA on, take a screenshot, see that it is.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nEDIT: made a small one which uses a horrible checkerboard shader to make foveation super obvious.\n[frag_dens_map_test.tar.gz](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/33235357/frag_dens_map_test.tar.gz)\n\n~~https://gitlab.com/DanielKinsman/foveated-render-test~~\n\n~~Sorry about the MRP size, needed a hard scene to render to make sure dynamic foveation would kick in~~","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124141/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":2},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124141/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}